  "slug": "halo-evolution-cdde",
  "summary": "New halo-modelling and N-body tools target Stage IV accuracy and LSST-scale data volumes with validation against established codes and fits.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational infrastructure linking dark matter halo evolution to survey observables. SciPIC-lite provides a public Python pipeline for flexible Halo Occupation Distribution modelling aimed at clustering observables, validated by fitting. PhotoNs-3 is tested against GADGET for accuracy and convergence in power spectra, halo profiles and mass functions, framed around Stage IV requirements. A separate N-body scheme for self-interacting dark matter uses distance-threshold interactions that depend on relative velocity and time step, targeting enhanced spatial resolution and performance. The supernova Woodbury factorization paper is related mainly through scale, reducing LSST-scale fit time from about 10 weeks to about 1.5 hr. Collectively, the emphasis is on validated, tractable pipelines rather than new halo-physics measurements.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
